    "description": {
      "value": "<p>You spent formative years in a scriptorium, a monastery dedicated to the preservation of knowledge, or a government agency, where you learned to write with a clear hand and produce finely written texts. Perhaps you scribed government documents or copied tomes of literature. You might have some skill as a writer of poetry, narrative, or scholarly research. Above all, you have a careful attention to detail, helping you avoid introducing mistakes to the documents you copy and create.</p><p><strong>Ability Scores:</strong> Dexterity, Intelligence, Wisdom</p><p><strong>Feat:</strong> @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.feats24.Item.phbftSkilled0000]{Skilled}</p><p><strong>Skill Proficiencies:</strong> Investigation and Perception</p><p><strong>Tool Proficiency:</strong> Calligrapher's Supplies</p><p><strong>Equipment:</strong> <em>Choose A or B:</em> (A) @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.equipment24.Item.phbtulCalligraph]{Calligrapher’s Supplies}, @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.equipment24.Item.phbagClothesFine]{Fine Clothes}, @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.equipment24.Item.phbagLamp0000000]{Lamp}, @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.equipment24.Item.phbagOil00000000]{Oil} (3 flasks), @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.equipment24.Item.phbagParchment00]{Parchment} (12 sheets), 23 GP; or (B) 50 GP</p>",
      "chat": ""
